PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel unanimously identifies the three sequential medications as valproic acid, topiramate, and lamotrigine, culminating in Stevens-Johnson syndrome/toxic epidermal necrolysis. The process leading to skin blisters is initiated pharmacokinetically by valproate-mediated inhibition of lamotrigine glucuronidation via UDP-glucuronosyltransferase (UGT1A4/2B7). Mechanistically, this clearance failure shunts accumulating lamotrigine toward cytochrome P450-mediated epoxidation to form reactive arene oxide intermediates that trigger immune-mediated epidermal detachment. Both glucuronidation (or its inhibition) and epoxidation remain the central, complementary answers across clinical and toxicological frameworks.
}

